<<~ ahu slot=`#/ground`>>

! Outbound Bridge ~ the one subscription that carries a live wiki change out

''Register: Model-Standing.'' Every claim below names a file and a line; a claim without one names itself as inference. The operator's words, verbatim (quote license): "(1) we don't use the syncer in our `lararium` vessels, but I suppose we should scout the back-parity flow there. (2) Write red-tests for this, we still work on cleaning up the architecture and re-founding in the parallel session. (3) daemon wiki projects to disk as `wikis/daemon`, and if it holds bags (it does have 'public system bags') can use residency verbs to move data to `bags/*`."

''What stands.'' Road B (#/back-parity), the ruled road: `packages/lararium-tw5/src/outbound-bridge.ts` `bridgeWikiToAdaptor` subscribes the wiki's `change` bus and reads each dispatch whole for `IslandAdaptor` (#/the-shore-law); `packages/lararium-tw5/src/sovereign-kernel.ts` stands ONE per island after `buildIslandRecipe` and cancels it at teardown (`_bridgeUnsub`). No `module-type: syncadaptor` ships and `$tw.syncer` never stands. An anchor placement into the daemon's own wiki leaves by the same listener. Witnesses: #/reds.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/the-shore-law`>>

!! The wiki-shore law ~ one act: a tiddler replaces a tiddler

''One act.'' Tiddlers stand as invariants, and every write replaces a tiddler under a title. A draft reads as an ordinary tiddler that carries `draft.of`, a convention of the editing surface: drafts belong to the surface. One storage act serves a draft and every other tiddler. The shore reads `draft.of` and `draft.title` for four things alone: the layer the cascade routes a draft to, the base a save carries, the titles that form one discrete act, and the body that persists whole (a draft never splits into slot children). The operator's words (quote license): "it's 'tiddlers as invariants' and every write replaces a tiddler. The 'Draft of X by Y' convention was created long ago for the UX surface."

Both of TiddlyWiki's edit roads meet this one act. The draft road (`tm-edit-tiddler` → a draft written on every input → `tm-save-tiddler`, `tm-cancel-tiddler`) and the direct road (`$edit-text`, `$checkbox`, `$action-setfield` and their kin writing straight to a title) each replace tiddlers under titles, and the shore serves both by the clauses below (`packages/lararium-tw5/src/island-adaptor.ts`, `outbound-bridge.ts`, `landed-ledger.ts`, `hand-gate.ts`, `draft-book.ts`, `wave-landing.ts`).

# ''Ask WHAT a tiddler says, never WHO moved it.'' The shore keeps a LANDED LEDGER: per title, the value the last wave left in the wiki, the bag it landed from and that bag's heads (`LandedLedger`, `landedOf(title)`). A `change` notification whose title holds the landed value reads as FOAM, and the bridge skips it where the title holds no pending hand; any other state reads as a HAND. Foam on a title that holds a hand re-marks the title, so the flush reads the state that stands at the flush. No origin flag, no change count and no list of expected titles takes part. The ledger lives in memory, one per shore: a shore turns resident when its seed wave has rebuilt the ledger, and a stopped shore clears it, so a restart reads the wiki afresh.
# ''What counts as content.'' Every persisted tiddler field counts, `modified`, `modifier` and `created` included. The host's provenance stamp `$origin-bag` and the store record's `meta` ceremony never compare. A program that re-adds a tiddler with nothing moved but `modified` writes a hand; the cure belongs at that program, never in a wider foam test.
# ''A hand leaves with its base.'' The base names the bag and the heads the hand built on: the heads the last wave landed for the title, or the heads the store returned for this shore's own last write of it (`writtenAt`). The store applies a based write at those heads and at FIELD grain: a field the hand left alone merges clean with a concurrent change to it, and a field both hands changed surfaces both values as parallel drafts. A removal counts as a change: where the hand removed a field a concurrent writer set, the concurrent value stays live and the hand's record, without that field, surfaces as a parallel draft (`lar-conflict-removed`) that its reader keeps BEFORE the hand's change lands, so a vessel that stops between the two still holds the hand's whole record; a removal no concurrent writer touched, and a removal both made, land clean. A typing run never conflicts with itself, since each returning write advances the base. A base outside the document's history retries without it.
# ''Pacing follows the hand's activity on a title, never the title's kind.'' An ordinary hand write marks its TITLE in one per-title gate (`HandGate`; a discrete act, next clause, takes its titles out of the gate): a trailing window of 400 ms under a non-resetting cap of 2 s. What leaves at the flush equals the title's state in the wiki at that flush (a direct caller that hands in a tiddler the wiki does not hold rides pinned, its value standing in). The timer paces and decides nothing: a hand that returned to the landed value inside its window writes nothing, a title the store never saw and the wiki does not hold raises no tombstone, a refused write arms no timer, and teardown flushes every marked title and drops none.
# ''A discrete act leaves in its turn.'' One `change` dispatch that holds the deletion of a draft the shore knows reads as a SAVE (the draft's target also written), a RENAME (`draft.title` names another title) or a CANCEL (the deletion alone). The act takes its titles out of the gate and issues its store calls inside the dispatch turn, one `writeFamily` per (bag, base), with no wait. A save builds on the base the draft opened on; a rename onto a standing title proceeds as an ordinary write on that title's landed base, and its source's tombstone lands in the source's own bag where that bag sits at or above the working layer, else where the composition's order shadows it from above; a cancel writes nothing for the target. One dispatch writes a target once.
# ''The draft carries its target's base from the moment it opened.'' The base persists on the draft's STORE record as `lar-draft-base-bag` and `lar-draft-base-heads`, so it follows the draft to another device and answers inside the dispatch that deletes the draft; a draft whose target no route can land persists with no base, and the target's refusal stands on the alert rail. The wiki's draft never holds the two fields, so an untouched draft reads unmodified and Cancel asks nothing. A target that moved between open and save merges at field grain: a field the draft left alone keeps the newer value, a field both hands changed surfaces both values, and nothing overwrites.
# ''A wave meets a hand at the landing.'' Before a queued change lands over a title that holds an unsent hand, the hand leaves first. When the store takes that write, the queued change yields to the write's own returning wave; when the hand owed nothing, the change lands. A plugin's shadow carries no hand: an unmarked shadow meets a wave as an empty title does, so a peer's record for a shadowed title lands over it.
# ''The wiki shows what the composition resolves.'' A bagged wave lands the topmost layer's record for its title, a tombstone included, with that layer's bag and heads. A lower layer's record never lands over a higher layer's, and a change beneath a working tombstone or copy-up never shows through.
# ''A hand lands at or above the working layer.'' The cascade names a layer and the composition's own order decides: a save lands in the layer the cascade names when the composition mounts it at or above the working layer, or in the higher layer where the title already lives. A delete of a title that landed beneath the working layer writes nothing there: its tombstone lands where a save of the title would (the temp layer for session state, the personal layer for a person's view state), else in the working layer. The write-layer pointer steers nothing into canon; a bag changes only by a residency move. The layer law in full: `lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/recipe-layer-model`.
# ''A refusal raises a named alert and the hand stays owed.'' A save the composition cannot land raises `$:/temp/lares/alert/unrouted-save/<pointer>`; a store write refused raises `$:/temp/lares/alert/unsaved/<title>`; a resident landing that fails twice raises `$:/temp/lares/alert/landing-failed/<title>` and retries on a later wave, while a seed landing that fails twice rejects the seed checkpoint; a parallel draft no draft layer could keep raises `$:/temp/lares/alert/parallel-draft/<draft>`. A refused hand write stays owed for the next change to the title, the next wave or teardown. The `landing-failed` and `unsaved` alerts clear on recovery; the `unrouted-save` alert stays on the rail.
# ''Two planes never persist.'' The volatile VM plane (`lar:///lararium.local.vm/…`) and the alert rail (`$:/temp/lares/alert/…`) take no store call, ahead of any cascade rule.
# ''One shore per engine.'' The shore installs the landing queue's door at `$tw.lares.enqueueNalu` and removes it at teardown; a second shore on one engine refuses by `LandingDoorOccupiedError`.

''No clock decides here.'' The pacing gate's two timers stand at the island's edge and only pace (`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/no-global-now`); the landing queue paces by host task and reads no duration.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/tw5-outbound-law`>>

!! How TiddlyWiki carries a live edit outward

The fork's own loop, `TiddlyWiki5/core/modules/syncer.js`, laid flat:

| leg | file:line | what it does |
|---|---|---|
| the subscription | `syncer.js:80-101` | `wiki.addEventListener("change", …)`: filters the changed titles through the sync filter; a non-empty result → `processTaskQueue()`; an empty result still queues when a `deleted` change names a title in `tiddlerInfo` (a known tiddler left) |
| the dispatch | `core/modules/wiki.js:144-170` (`enqueueTiddlerEvent`) | every `addTiddler`/`deleteTiddler` bumps `changeCount[title]` and schedules ONE `dispatchEvent("change", changes)` on `$tw.utils.nextTick` (`core/modules/utils/utils.js:706` → `process.nextTick` on node, `setTimeout 0` in a browser). The event fires AFTER the synchronous caller returns — never inside it |
| the filter of what leaves | `syncer.js:19`, `:67`, `:165`; `core/wiki/config/SyncFilter.tid` | `$:/config/SyncFilter` compiles once: `[is[tiddler]] -[[$:/core]] -[[$:/library/sjcl.js]] -[prefix[$:/boot/]] -[prefix[$:/HistoryList]] -[status[pending]plugin-type[import]] -[[$:/isEncrypted]] -[prefix[$:/status/]] -[prefix[$:/state/]] -[prefix[$:/temp/]]` — TOTAL minus a NAMED exclusion list |
| the dirty set | `syncer.js:181-199` (`readTiddlerInfo`), `:204-238` (`isDirty`) | `tiddlerInfo[title] = { revision, changeCount, adaptorInfo, timestampLastSaved }`; dirty = a synced title whose `wiki.getChangeCount(title)` exceeds its recorded `changeCount`, or unknown to the adaptor, or known and now absent (a pending delete) |
| the throttle | `syncer.js:23-27`, `:478-521` (`chooseNextTask`) | `throttleInterval` 1 s (`$:/config/SyncThrottleInterval`): a title saved within the last second waits; `taskTimerInterval` 250 ms re-polls; `errorRetryInterval` 5 s; one task in flight at a time (`numTasksInProgress`, `:425`). Order: saves · a server sync · deletes · lazy loads |
| the save task | `syncer.js:535-561` | `syncadaptor.saveTiddler(tiddler, cb, { tiddlerInfo })`; on success records `{ changeCount, adaptorInfo, revision, timestampLastSaved }` |
| the delete task | `syncer.js:573-588` | `syncadaptor.deleteTiddler(title, cb, { tiddlerInfo })`; on success deletes `tiddlerInfo[title]`. The adaptor receives the LAST-KNOWN `adaptorInfo` — the tiddler itself has gone |
| the echo law | `syncer.js:254-264` (`storeTiddler`) | an INBOUND tiddler lands through `wiki.addTiddler` and stamps `tiddlerInfo[title].changeCount = wiki.getChangeCount(title)` in the same synchronous stretch — so the `change` that fires next tick reads no delta and queues no save. The guard rides the COUNT, never a flag |
| the adaptor contract | `startup.js:104-118`; `filesystemadaptor.js:25-140`; `tiddlywebadaptor.js:26-275` | `module-type: syncadaptor`, `exports.adaptorClass`; `name` · `supportsLazyLoading` · `isReady()` · `getTiddlerInfo(tiddler)` · `saveTiddler(tiddler, cb, opts)` · `loadTiddler(title, cb)` · `deleteTiddler(title, cb, opts)`; optional `getStatus`/`login`/`logout`/`getUpdatedTiddlers`/`getSkinnyTiddlers`/`getTiddlerRevision`. The FIRST module of the type wins; `$tw.syncer` stands only when one registers (`:112`) |
| `$:/status/IsLoggedIn` | `syncer.js:15`, `:269-283` | written by `getStatus`; `tm-login`/`tm-logout` ride the root widget (`:115-128`, browser only) |
| the hooks | `core/modules/widgets/navigator.js:248`, `:255`, `:332` | `th-deleting-tiddler` and `th-saving-tiddler` fire in the NAVIGATOR on a UI save/delete — they gate the widget's act, never the syncer's; a programmatic `addTiddler` never passes them |

Two facts the stock adaptors carry that the island's shape already mirrors: the filesystem adaptor keeps `$tw.boot.files[title]` as its siting memory and reads it on delete (`filesystemadaptor.js:128-131`); the tiddlyweb adaptor reads `options.tiddlerInfo.adaptorInfo.bag` on delete and skips a title the server never saw (`tiddlywebadaptor.js:264-268`) — the syncer's `tiddlerInfo` acts as a last-known-bag map, the office the island's landed ledger holds when it names the bag a title landed from.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/island-holds`>>

!! What the island holds in the syncer's place, and where the seam sits

| leg | where | what stands |
|---|---|---|
| the subscription | `packages/lararium-tw5/src/outbound-bridge.ts` `bridgeWikiToAdaptor` | one `change` listener per island; it reads each dispatch whole: discrete acts first (`handleChangeDispatch`), then every other title as foam or a hand |
| the outbound save | `packages/lararium-tw5/src/island-adaptor.ts` `saveTiddler` → `HandGate.mark` → `_flushHandImpl` → `_writeMeme` | the volatile plane and the alert rail refuse first; the title marks the per-title gate; the flush reads the title's state, settles its bag (`_saveBag`) and its base (`_basePlan`), and lands the meme family through `store.writeFamily(…, { bag, base })` with `$origin-bag` stripped |
| the outbound delete | `island-adaptor.ts` `deleteTiddler` → `_flushHandImpl` → `_tombstoneBag` | the bag of this shore's own last acknowledged write of the title answers first, then the landed ledger's bag; the composition's layer order then picks the tombstone's bag; `tombstoneInBag(bag, title, origin, { base })` |
| the filter of what leaves | `packages/lararium-tw5/tiddlers/lar-bag-paths.tid` walked by `_routeBag`, settled by `_settle` | the cascade takes `SyncFilter`'s SHAPE (total, named exclusions) and adds a ROUTE per kind; a withholding stops a write only from a rule that names it; a gap lands at `current-wiki-bag` and warns; a route beneath the working layer, through an empty pointer or into an unmounted bag refuses by name |
| the echo law | `packages/lararium-tw5/src/landed-ledger.ts`; `island-adaptor.ts` `isFoam`, `holdsHand` | content against the landed value (#/the-shore-law, clause 1) |
| the inbound half | `onUriChanged` → the landing queue (`wave-landing.ts`) → `_landOne` → `$tw.lares.applyNalu` (`modules/nalu-engine.ts`) | every envelope joins one queue; each landing resolves its title through the composition (`resolveLayered`), meets any unsent hand, applies, and records the result in the ledger; `$origin-bag` rides from the envelope |
| who calls the outbound methods | `outbound-bridge.ts` (the `change` listener `sovereign-kernel.ts` holds) and the tests | the one production caller |

''The seam.'' `packages/lararium-tw5/src/sovereign-kernel.ts` keeps `buildIslandRecipe`'s `adaptor` and hands it to `bridgeWikiToAdaptor(tw5, adaptor)`, the one `$tw.wiki.addEventListener("change", …)` the island holds, cancelled at teardown after the kernel awaits the wiki's queued dispatch (`awaitWikiDispatch`), so an edit whose notification had not fired reaches `stop()` as a marked hand. No `module-type: syncadaptor` ships in the plugin, so `$tw.syncer` never stands (`tw5-vm.ts` names the syncer as discarded on purpose).

''Why no flag can serve, MEASURED'' (`packages/lararium-tw5/tests/outbound-bridge.test.ts` "CONTROL (5b)"): `change` dispatches on `nextTick`, AFTER an apply lowered `isApplyingNalu()`. Inside a `change` listener the flag reads `false` for every inbound apply, so it tells a SYNCHRONOUS caller alone. TW5's own `changeCount` lives in memory and a set of expected titles goes stale across a multi-change apply; the landed ledger asks only what stands, so one answer serves a live wave, a seed and a restart.

''The anchor placement.'' `packages/lararium-tw5/src/meme-verbs.ts` `anchorBagOf` names the daemon's mounted working layer from `current-wiki-bag` and sinks through `wikiMemeSink(opts.tw5.$tw.wiki)` — a wiki write, which the bridge carries outward like any other. Witnessed through the daemon's own door (`tests/e2e/outbound-bridge.e2e.test.ts` B1): after `lares meme put <uri> --recipe default`, `meme get <uri> --bag lar:///ha.ka.ba/wikis/daemon/working` answers the meme.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/back-parity`>>

!! Back-parity ~ the ONE contract, and the two roads

''The contract both a stock `syncadaptor` and the island's adaptor MUST satisfy:''

# ''Save.'' A changed tiddler the filter admits reaches `saveTiddler(tiddler)` once per settled burst, with the title's state read at the flush. Stock: the 1 s throttle + `changeCount` delta. Island: the per-title pacing gate, whose flush reads the title's state, and the discrete act that leaves in its turn (#/the-shore-law). Both coalesce; neither drops.
# ''Delete.'' A gone title reaches the delete path after the wiki lost its fields, so the adaptor answers from what it knew LAST. Stock: the syncer hands over `options.tiddlerInfo.adaptorInfo` (`syncer.js:586`). Island: `deleteTiddler(title)` reads the bag of the shore's last acknowledged write of the title, else the landed ledger's bag, and the composition's layer order settles where the tombstone lands (`_tombstoneBag`).
# ''The dirty/echo law.'' An inbound apply MUST NOT re-save. Stock: the `changeCount` stamp at `storeTiddler`. Island: the landed ledger (#/the-shore-law, clause 1) — a `change` listener cannot read `isApplyingNalu()` raised, so parity rides WHAT STANDS, never a flag.
# ''The filter of what leaves the wiki.'' Total minus named exclusions. Stock: `$:/config/SyncFilter`. Island: the cascade's withholding rules (`lar-bag-paths.tid`) — plus a ROUTE, which the stock filter never carries.

''Road A — register the island's adaptor as `module-type: syncadaptor` and let TW5's own syncer drive it.''

* Gains: the subscription, the throttle, the dirty set, `isDirty()`/`tc-dirty`, the beforeunload warning, the `tm-server-refresh` hook, and the `changeCount` echo law arrive as the fork's own code — parity by RIDING the loop, tested upstream. `$:/config/SyncFilter` and `$:/config/SyncThrottleInterval` become operator dials. The adaptor gains `getTiddlerInfo` (`{ bag }` — the slot the cascade named) and `deleteTiddler` reads it from `options.tiddlerInfo.adaptorInfo.bag`, leaving the delete's bag to the syncer's map.
* Costs: the adaptor must ship INSIDE the plugin as a TW5 module — a packed CJS module reaching `@lararium/mesh` by subpath (`modules/nalu-engine.ts` names the law) with NO access to the composite it writes to unless the kernel hands it through `$tw.lares` (the way `applyNalu` rides). The syncer's callback shape `(err, adaptorInfo, revision)` wraps the promise. The syncer polls `SyncFromServerTask` every 60 s (`pollTimerInterval`) — a no-op without `getUpdatedTiddlers`, but a timer that runs. `SyncFilter` excludes `$:/state/`, `$:/temp/`, `$:/status/` OUTRIGHT, where the cascade ROUTES them to the temp store — so the temp slot goes unfed without a per-island override of the filter. The syncer applies the same law to the daemon island and the wiki island alike (one plugin), and `$tw.syncer` stands as a global the browser vessel inherits. Two loops (nalu inbound, syncer outbound) hold two dirty/echo laws.
* Where it lands: `plugins/` (a new packed module) · `sovereign-kernel.ts` (hand the composite to `$tw.lares`) · `island-adaptor.ts` (the callback shore).

''Road B — keep the direct listener; parity by shape.''

* Gains: one subscription in the kernel (`sovereign-kernel.ts` after `buildIslandRecipe`), the adaptor's routing and the cascade's temp route kept, no packed module, no syncer global, no poll timer. The echo law lives at the shore as the landed ledger: content decides, so one law serves a live wave, a seed and a restart.
* Costs: the dirty set, `isDirty()`, the unload warning and `tc-dirty` stay OWED to the island. Every upstream change to `syncer.js` demands a fresh reading and a re-spelling by hand — parity by shape drifts the way every hand-derived enumeration drifts. The `SyncFilter` dial stays absent; the cascade alone says what leaves.
* Where it lands: `sovereign-kernel.ts` (the subscription + teardown) · `outbound-bridge.ts` (the dispatch read whole) · `island-adaptor.ts` (the ledger, the gate, the acts).

''RULED: Road B'' (`scale-stories-basket-one#/the-bridge`): `outbound-bridge.ts` carries it, with the echo law read from the landed ledger. Road A stays costed above as the road not taken; the witnesses in #/reds hold the five-clause contract either road would owe.

''VERIFIED (`G10`): every leaked change routes as a save.'' `wiki-shore-echo-law.test.ts` reads an inbound landing's echo as zero store calls, behind a barrier (the dispatch, the gate's fire, the landing queue's idle), and proves that zero with a known positive in the same dispatch: four leaked titles and a hand edit over the inbound title each route as a save into the working layer, and a vanished title routes as a tombstone. Foam routes nothing; a leak always routes.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/daemon-mirror`>>

!! The daemon wiki projects to `wikis/daemon/` ~ the grant, the seam, the residency door

''What stands.'' `packages/lararium-node/src/disk-projector.ts` carries NO exclusion by name — a bag absent from `mirrors` never writes; the daemon's mirrors arrive as GRANTS like any wiki island's. `packages/lararium-node/src/open-daemon-vm.ts` hands `openDaemonVmCore` a `diskMirrors` list (`daemonWorkingMirror(rootDir)` plus `bags/crossroads`), `packages/lararium-tw5/src/daemon-vm-core.ts` carries it onto the manifest, and `packages/lararium-node/src/node-daemon-island.ts` passes `onBoot: (ctx) => mountDiskProjection(manifest, ctx)` — the ONE mount `packages/lararium-node/src/island-behaviors.ts` also gives a wiki island. `bags/daemon` (the control plane) stays mirrorless: no grant names it.

''The grant shape, minted and witnessed'' (`packages/lararium-node/src/bag-paths.ts` `daemonWorkingMirror(rootDir)` → `{ bagId: lar:///ha.ka.ba/wikis/daemon/working, mirrorRoot: <root>/wikis/daemon }`): the shape `resolveDiskMirrors` (`packages/lararium-mesh/src/vessel-island-pool-core.ts`) fills for every wiki's `wikiSlot: "working"` grant from the slug at mount; the daemon mounts outside the pool, so the mint stands by name. Witness `packages/lararium-node/tests/daemon-working-mirror.test.ts`: the shape · a record in `wikis/daemon/working` projects to `<root>/wikis/daemon/<uri-path>.mem` · CONTROL: `bags/daemon` projects NOWHERE · the MOVE's unlink leg: a carrier that LEFT the working layer unlinks from `wikis/daemon/` and a carrier held there stays (`disk-projector.ts` `_scheduleUnlinkByTitle`, `bagsHolding`).

''The seam.'' `open-daemon-vm.ts` mints the daemon's mirrors under the vessel root — `daemonWorkingMirror(rootDir)` beside `bags/crossroads` (the public system bag the daemon holds, by the operator's word; the crossroads grant carries `guardNexusHandles`, which only a proven charter identity lifts) — and hands them to `openDaemonVmCore` → `mkManifest(…, { diskMirrors })`; `node-daemon-island.ts` passes `onBoot: (ctx) => mountDiskProjection(manifest, ctx)` as the `makeOperatorDaemonBehavior` OPTION (the seat that also lights the projection cap — an `onBoot` on the returned behavior object mounts nothing), and `island-behaviors.ts` lifts the wiki island's mount into that ONE `mountDiskProjection` both entries call. Witness (`tests/e2e/outbound-bridge.e2e.test.ts` "★ the daemon wiki projects: a record in wikis/daemon/working lands at <root>/wikis/daemon/<uri-path>.mem ★"): a DIRECT `meme put --bag lar:///ha.ka.ba/wikis/daemon/working` projects to `<root>/wikis/daemon/<uri-path>.mem`. The fixture names a three-term root (`ha.ka.ba/t/bridge/…`): the siting law sites `lar:///w.w.w/…` names alone (`carrierBaseRelPath`), so a one-term root such as `lar:///t/bridge/direct` would project nowhere and read as a dead mirror.

''The residency door'' (`tests/e2e/meme-live-contact.test.ts` "★ act MOVE --from wikis/daemon/working --to bags/crossroads — the residency verb carries a daemon-wiki carrier out ★"): `lares act MOVE --title <uri> --from lar:///ha.ka.ba/wikis/daemon/working --to lar:///ha.ka.ba/bags/crossroads --yes` answers `ok`; the cap gate refused NOTHING — `attachDaemonWorking` registers the working slot with keyhive and delegates it to the seated face (`packages/lararium-keyhive/src/operator-daemon-behavior.ts`); after the MOVE `meme get --bag wikis/daemon/working` answers `not-found` and `meme get --bag bags/crossroads` answers the carrier. The CRDT leg stands whole.

''The disk leg of that MOVE'' (the same suite, "★ the daemon designates crossroads: the MOVE publishes under bags/crossroads/ and leaves wikis/daemon/ ★"): `bags/crossroads/` stands as a GRANT on the node's mirror list (`open-node-vessel.ts`, authority), and no wiki recipe DESIGNATES it — `packages/lararium-tw5/src/vessel-steps.ts` `PRIMARY_MIRROR_BAGS` names lares and lararium, to which each wiki adds its own working slot and its own bag, and never crossroads. The daemon holds the public system bags, so the DAEMON designates crossroads in its own mirror set (`open-daemon-vm.ts`); the MOVE publishes under `<root>/bags/crossroads/ha.ka.ba/t/witness/move.mem` and unlinks `<root>/wikis/daemon/…`.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/reds`>>

!! The witnesses, one per clause

Every vector below runs as a plain `test` and stands GREEN; each carries, as its assertion message, the failure it would print were its wire cut, so a regression names the clause it broke.

| # | suite · vector | clause | the failure it names |
|---|---|---|---|
| 1 | `packages/lararium-tw5/tests/outbound-bridge.test.ts` "(1) SEAM `change`→saveTiddler: `$tw.wiki.addTiddler` of a plain title → `store.put` in working, `$origin-bag` stripped" | 1 SAVE | `no put reached the store — nothing carries the wiki's change event to saveTiddler` |
| 2 | "(2) … a tiddler whose `draft.of` stands → `store.put` in the draft slot" | 1 SAVE, draft route | `the draft never reached the store` |
| 3 | "(3) a saved draft deletion uses the draft bag after the wiki title is gone" | 2 DELETE | `the delete never reached the store — the record resurrects on the next boot` |
| 4 | "(4) … `$:/temp/*` → the temp store, never a CRDT put" | 4 FILTER | `the volatile write never reached the composite` |
| 5 | "CONTROL (5): a nalu-applied inbound change fires NO outbound put" | 3 ECHO | an inbound apply that re-saves |
| 5b | "CONTROL (5b) MEASURED: `change` dispatches after the drain lowered `isApplyingNalu`" | 3 ECHO, its evidence | the reason the echo law reads what stands and never the flag |
| 6 | "(6) SEAM anchor→store: `$tw.lares.meme.place` (the anchor `meme put`, no target) → its records reach the working store" | 5 ANCHOR | `the anchor placement stands in $tw.wiki alone` |
| B1 | `tests/e2e/outbound-bridge.e2e.test.ts` "B1 the bridge (Road B): the explicit anchor recipe reaches the daemon working store" | 5 ANCHOR, through the daemon's door | `the anchor placement stands in $tw.wiki alone` |
| B2 | `tests/e2e/outbound-bridge.e2e.test.ts` "the daemon wiki projects: a record in wikis/daemon/working lands at <root>/wikis/daemon/<uri-path>.mem" | the daemon mirror (#/daemon-mirror) | `nothing projected at <root>/wikis/daemon/…` |
| M | `tests/e2e/meme-live-contact.test.ts` "the daemon designates crossroads: the MOVE publishes under bags/crossroads/ and leaves wikis/daemon/" | the residency door | `the MOVE never published under <root>/bags/crossroads/…` |

The shore law's own vectors stand beside these in `packages/lararium-tw5/tests/`: `wiki-shore-vectors` (foam, the base, the wave that meets a hand, the seed checkpoint, the returning hand) · `wiki-shore-draft-road` (save, rename, cancel, the draft-open base across devices) · `wiki-shore-field-grain` · `wiki-shore-cross-bag` · `wiki-shore-shadow` and `wiki-shore-route` (where a hand's save and delete land) · `wiki-shore-returning-hand`, `wiki-shore-faults` and `wiki-shore-landing-failed` (the alerts and what stays owed) · `wiki-shore-residue` · `draft-reads-unmodified`.

CONTROLS standing green beside them: an explicit `--recipe default` put lands in the daemon's wiki and reads back · a DIRECT put into `wikis/daemon/working` lands and reads back through the same bag · `bags/daemon/` never appears under the root · the MOVE out of the daemon wiki answers `ok` and the carrier reads back from crossroads.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/remains`>>

!! What remains, named

* ''`isDirty` · the unload warning · `tc-dirty`'' — the syncer's UI legs, which Road B does not carry; owed to the island.
* ''`wiki.transact`'' — the fork ships none (`grep transact TiddlyWiki5/core` reaches nothing) and the nalu engine calls none: every landing applies one tiddler, and `change` gathers titles by TW5's own `nextTick` schedule alone.

<<~/ahu>>

